WEBVTT

1
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.550
The village of Dulin Brijeg lies right on the edge of the Tara River canyon,

2
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.180
at an altitude of 1380 metres.

3
00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:57.680
It has only three residents, among them Srđan.

4
00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.180
Srđan is originally from the village of Velenići, the hamlet of Podgrad.

5
00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:07.310
Until 2019 he lived in Foča, and then he decides to begin a new chapter in his life.

6
00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:11.180
On his ancestral land he decides to build something special.

7
00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:18.790
Here I am in the village of Dulin Brijeg. Only three people live here.

8
00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:22.410
I came with Srđan, to ride a bit through the Tara River canyon.

9
00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:26.610
This area belongs to the municipality of Foča and borders the municipality of Pljevlja,

10
00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:30.160
so just three kilometres from the border with Montenegro.

11
00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:34.680
The first impression is fascinating. We have a view of Durmitor, Ljubišnja is behind us.

12
00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.140
What else do we have? A view of Maglić. Paradise on earth if you ask me.

13
00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:09.670
I spent a lot of time on the river as a skipper, and I slightly missed staying in the canyon itself,

14
00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:23.680
so I came here, to the very edge of the canyon, where my roots come from, to try to build something for myself.

15
00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:28.060
What did the others say when you said you'd be here?

16
00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.180
Well, that I'm crazy.

17
00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:55.110
We have an altitude difference of about 900 metres.

18
00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:55.780
900 metres.

19
00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:47.340
Absolutely, I came up with the idea of starting something touristic

20
00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:52.610
and making it different from the offer down there, that is, the campsites.

21
00:03:52.610 --> 00:04:02.570
They all have that rafting and are oriented, let's say, towards Prijevor and Zelengora, which is again quite far to drive.

22
00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:09.970
Then I came with the idea, I said to myself, I'll have something on offer that others in this area don't have.

23
00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.530
What could it be? Horses.

24
00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:18.810
I had no idea what I was getting into, I thought it was a lot easier.

25
00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:28.540
Talking to people down on the river, you see that a lot of people come for rafting, and they would look for something other than rafting.

26
00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:33.480
So, by chance, Podgrad is on the very edge of the Tara River canyon,

27
00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:39.020
so I got the idea to try something in the village, something new in our area,

28
00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:41.380
and then the horse came to my mind.

29
00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:46.640
I had absolutely no contact with them.

30
00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:56.070
In the very first year I even broke my arm right away, when I went after somebody else's horse down in the meadow,

31
00:04:56.070 --> 00:05:00.140
and I broke my arm in four places.

32
00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.530
Do you have love for horses?

33
00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:14.830
I do, of course I do. Had it not been for the horses, I'm still convinced nothing would have worked out,

34
00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:19.620
because the horses always drove me to go out to the village, both when you can and when you can't.

35
00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:26.890
Are you sure on the horses when we go along the cliff, when we ride?

36
00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:35.200
A million percent. If I weren't sure, I wouldn't risk, let's say, neither myself nor anybody else.

37
00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:38.520
There have never been any problems.

38
00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:48.990
There was absolutely nothing, forest, forest and a village that then had no residents.

39
00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:55.830
The forest hid this view that we have here now.

40
00:05:55.830 --> 00:06:06.160
Everybody told me: where are you going there, water is far, the road is far, what will you do there.

41
00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:33.460
Until 2012 there were a few more people, and the last family left in 2017.

42
00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:39.840
This whole district, Velenići, Čelebići, Meštrevac, had an eight-year school.

43
00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:54.600
In less than twenty years the population dispersed, moved down to the city.

44
00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:57.400
This place is called Podgrad,

45
00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:01.610
not far from us there is the foundation of a church from the late Middle Ages

46
00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:05.160
and they say it was the centre of the region in that period.

47
00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:12.640
This place was called Grad, and these houses were built under that rock, which is why the hamlet is called Podgrad.

48
00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:29.560
The town of Rogatica had a horse stud farm.

49
00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:33.810
That stud farm was founded in 1896, Austria-Hungary founded it.

50
00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:38.800
For the needs of their army they were looking for horses best suited for long-distance riding,

51
00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:40.020
and that is the Arabian horse.

52
00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:45.990
And then they brought many purebred Arabian horses from Syria and used them in these lands of ours.

53
00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:48.950
However, later they saw the flaws of this horse.

54
00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:55.610
That horse didn't tolerate our winter very well, and its hoof was too soft for the ground in these lands of ours.

55
00:07:56.130 --> 00:08:03.480
And then they started to breed a horse that has to stay in the type of the Arabian horse in looks, in temperament, in those riding characteristics,

56
00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:07.610
only for genetics to add resistance to winter and a firmer hoof.

57
00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:19.220
There were 8 Arabian head, 3 stallions and 5 mares, and there were over 20 Bosnian mountain horses and some crossbreeds.

58
00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:03.520
Evening is falling so you put the foals away, let's see.

59
00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:08.370
We're now shutting in these two foals that we bought recently.

60
00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:16.460
And since the horses were bought, they're young and weren't born here, my herd hasn't accepted them yet.

61
00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:23.930
So I'm afraid, in case wild animals come, I'm afraid whether the herd would defend them.

62
00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:29.770
And so I shut in only those two foals at night, and in the morning I let them out.

63
00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:31.800
And can the others defend themselves?

64
00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:36.870
The others, here we have two more foals that were born here, and the mothers are here too,

65
00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:43.750
then they group together, and I'm afraid for these foals, whether they would be defended if something happens.

66
00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:46.870
What if a wolf came across a big herd?

67
00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:48.610
Well, they would group together.

68
00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:53.600
But still, last spring there was a situation where I had a problem.

69
00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:57.910
But a wolf is clever, he plans an attack, he's no fool, he doesn't rush.

70
00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:02.830
He waits for his moment and is ready to wait for hours, as they say.

71
00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:13.750
The horses are very rarely in the stable, during some rains, when the temperature is below five degrees, only then do I shut them in while it's falling.

72
00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:19.610
I joke when I tell the horses: what shall we do, how shall we do it, and they say: you're a bit unserious,

73
00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:23.300
first build us a roof over our heads, you'll manage somehow.

74
00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:27.250
And so the first building that was built here was the stable.

75
00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:38.680
Srđan says, we get up at half past four.

76
00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:42.270
He says, we leave at five, we're setting off so I can show you my area.

77
00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:42.620
Let's go.

78
00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:54.720
We woke up nicely. We're going up to that peak. In the fog.

79
00:10:54.720 --> 00:11:00.030
The plan was to greet the sunrise at the top.

80
00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:08.210
During the walk we came across wild blueberries, helped ourselves and went on.

81
00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:15.540
When we have fog or a cloud like this beneath us, that's a temperature inversion.

82
00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:23.940
So that means the temperature down there is colder than here where we are now.

83
00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:33.200
We made it, right, Srki? Here, we've arrived at Čukavica.

84
00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:39.060
We were half an hour late, huh? Well, a little late, but...

85
00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:42.340
But it's never too late for the mountain.

86
00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:48.300
We're on the mountain Radovina and its peak Čukavica.

87
00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:58.390
This is good, look, this is the inversion.

88
00:11:58.390 --> 00:12:05.710
There's Ljubišnja, there's a cloud snagged on it.

89
00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:14.600
Durmitor, there it is, it's opening up. It looks like it will open up.

90
00:12:56.040 --> 00:13:00.380
Hikers come here to Radovina very rarely.

91
00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:07.670
I can't say they don't come at all, but it's much less visited than Ljubišnja.

92
00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:14.310
But it's very beautiful, brother. It's very beautiful and quite, let's say,

93
00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:21.140
and even for those hikers who aren't overly active, it's easy to climb.

94
00:13:21.140 --> 00:13:26.880
There are horses, bulls and oxen.

95
00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:40.200
People drive them away from home when spring comes, and then bring them back in autumn.

96
00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:50.380
Here, we found a herd of cattle. No horses, but there are cattle.

97
00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:19.660
This is the foals' field and now we're heading to the horse field.

98
00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:23.280
We're going down to the horse field.

99
00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:29.880
A perfect place for a break and a refresh by a spring.

100
00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:36.730
Here we are at the horse field. Our vehicle is waiting for us here.

101
00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:44.210
The guys drove it here and now we're going back to Srđa's house.

102
00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:06.700
Whose vehicle is this? A Volkswagen Iltis. What year? 1983.

103
00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:10.560
Is it a convertible like this from the factory?

104
00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:20.910
Yes, except it has its own canvas top and doors. The top is, let's say, old and a new one has to be made.

105
00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:24.660
We have the doors, but here, we don't use them.

106
00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:24.130
I switch it to four-wheel drive when needed, otherwise it's only rear-wheel drive.

107
00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:28.240
I'm curious, do you like driving it?

108
00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:50.480
Well, I like it, I like it. It's quite a specific vehicle, for smaller groups of people, up to four, five people, and it's extremely capable, and with it you can really tour beautiful terrain in this area of ours.

109
00:16:50.480 --> 00:17:04.260
You can go up to Radovina too, you can drive through these forest terrains where not every vehicle can get to.

110
00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:11.240
This vehicle was driven by a famous Foča car mechanic, Slobodan Starović,

111
00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:17.960
and he got it from the Orthodox church, and the church from the German embassy.

112
00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:24.260
He worked as a mechanic in his workshop, he drove exclusively this vehicle,

113
00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:32.070
when he retired he wanted to sell it, he had many interested people, especially hunters,

114
00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:38.880
and then he offered it to me first and I accepted his offer and now it's with me.

115
00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:27.030
In 2020 Srđan builds a road to his estate at his own expense.

116
00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:33.960
My road was dug at the end of 2020, and put into use in May of 21,

117
00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:41.650
because when it was dug there was mud, so it had to be filled in, so we waited for spring of 21.

118
00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:46.900
And then it was filled in and put into use in May 2021.

119
00:19:46.900 --> 00:20:05.380
Because with the road I had, I would have to go 45 kilometres to Foča, and then 25 kilometres to the rafting camps or another 20 kilometres to the rafting starting point.

120
00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:08.900
And now I'm 9 km from the starting point.

121
00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:15.450
And the wish of my late father was for the road through the Tara canyon to reach our village.

122
00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:22.100
At the same time I fulfilled that wish of his, which he told me on his deathbed.

123
00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:49.050
People have always been looking for places to rest that are far from the city crowds.

124
00:20:49.050 --> 00:21:01.320
That is exactly what guided Srđan when he decided to build bungalows meant for tourists who love peace and quiet.

125
00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:12.310
Right now we have here, let's say, seven accommodation units for guests, four-bed ones, all with bathrooms.

126
00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:19.400
There's a kitchen, there's this bungalow where the workers are housed, and this year a swimming pool was built too.

127
00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:37.980
When people came and dug the foundations for the restaurant and the kitchen and this bungalow where the workers live, the hole for the pool was dug as well.

128
00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:42.850
A stove arrived, some boiler, we want to heat the pool.

129
00:21:42.850 --> 00:21:50.620
It will be finished in some ten days, so at the beginning of October there will be water in the pool.

130
00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:52.480
Will it be possible to swim in winter?

131
00:21:52.480 --> 00:21:53.870
We hope so.

132
00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:59.750
And what temperature can you reach in the pool? Well, the water will be 23, 24 degrees.

133
00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:03.620
And what do you heat with? Wood. Wood, thank God there's plenty.

134
00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:08.650
We have two boilers, big ones, and some kind of tank.

135
00:22:08.650 --> 00:22:19.020
A thick pipe was laid down there, two pipes to the pool, and the water will circulate into the boiler and return to the pool.

136
00:22:19.020 --> 00:22:24.280
And the boiler room will be here? The boiler room will be here, yes.

137
00:22:24.280 --> 00:22:32.610
Really, in summer there are quite a few moments when it's really hot and you simply can't ride or hike in that heat.

138
00:22:32.610 --> 00:22:37.700
Someone goes rafting, someone simply stays here, enjoys, swims a bit, sunbathes,

139
00:22:37.700 --> 00:22:41.560
toward evening you ride the horses, or early in the morning, and that's it.

140
00:22:54.190 --> 00:23:09.400
And while Srđan finishes the day at the pool and cools off, I warm myself by the fire and that's the end of the day, we continue tomorrow.

141
00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:16.360
Well, let's go and try Srđan's famous zipline.

142
00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:30.700
The approach to the zipline is a small via ferrata; so we go through the small ferrata to get to the zipline, and we set off.

143
00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:36.060
Work on the ferrata started in the autumn of 22.

144
00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:40.610
That was the approach ferrata for the zip.

145
00:23:40.610 --> 00:23:44.900
And the zip was put into operation in June 23.

146
00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:49.190
And there's the view of the Tara canyon too.

147
00:23:49.190 --> 00:24:04.010
Well, now we come to the suspension bridge that we need to cross and that connects two rocks.

148
00:24:04.010 --> 00:24:15.820
This will hold all of us together, but the rule is one at a time.

149
00:24:32.130 --> 00:24:39.290
Canyon of the Tara both here and there.

150
00:24:39.290 --> 00:24:48.320
I've always loved these suspension bridges.

151
00:24:48.320 --> 00:25:11.930
We have one more small bridge, a ladder, and we reach the end of the ferrata and the beginning of the zipline.

152
00:25:16.030 --> 00:25:27.970
We're on the rock Gradina, which is also the start of our zipline, and we'll fly 308 metres to the rock Šupljica, where the zipline ends.

153
00:25:27.970 --> 00:25:43.010
And beneath us is the fastest part of the Tara river, we have the Borovi rapid, the most dangerous, the most demanding rapid on the river; below it come Varda, Ćelije, the Mlađički rapid and the Vjernovski rapid.

154
00:25:43.010 --> 00:25:49.880
By the way, those rapids, you see now how much water is missing, how much bank, let's say, without water.

155
00:25:49.880 --> 00:25:58.470
And in general, in May, from the start of Borovi to the exit from Vjernovići, in most cases it's practically one single rapid.

156
00:25:59.890 --> 00:26:04.030
Don't put a lot of pressure on the pulley, because it slows you down.

157
00:26:04.030 --> 00:26:07.570
So, try to leave some slack, one hand over the other.

158
00:26:07.570 --> 00:26:11.040
You decide which is your lower and which is your upper hand.

159
00:26:11.040 --> 00:26:15.240
Usually the upper hand is the one we work, eat and write with.

160
00:26:15.240 --> 00:26:18.320
So, as long as you're moving forward, let go of your hands.

161
00:26:18.320 --> 00:26:23.520
The moment you stop, if you haven't reached the end, the upper hand goes on the brake,

162
00:26:23.520 --> 00:26:28.530
you just lower it down or hold on with three percent of your strength so you don't start going backwards.

163
00:26:28.530 --> 00:26:31.300
That's it, are you ready?

164
00:26:31.300 --> 00:26:32.160
Ready.

165
00:26:32.160 --> 00:26:36.530
Three. Let's go, God help me. One. Zero. Bye.

166
00:27:15.890 --> 00:27:21.410
For the future, to expand the accommodation capacity a bit more,

167
00:27:21.410 --> 00:27:24.360
to around fifty beds,

168
00:27:24.360 --> 00:27:31.300
and then, as they say, to offer comfort too to the guests who will be here.

169
00:27:31.300 --> 00:27:35.870
Whether there will also be a sauna, things like that,

170
00:27:35.870 --> 00:27:41.010
and probably some more serious ferrata will be built.

171
00:27:41.010 --> 00:27:44.240
There will be some more ideas and plans here.

172
00:27:55.350 --> 00:27:59.620
Still, this here, the Tara River canyon, is the most beautiful.

173
00:27:59.620 --> 00:28:02.830
And all this is some additional activity,

174
00:28:02.830 --> 00:28:14.850
but in my opinion, above all, the people who come here should get to know both the river and the canyon in the right way.

175
00:28:16.190 --> 00:28:22.010
But really, in the city it's the same story, all the same questions. You're quite limited.

176
00:28:22.010 --> 00:28:34.230
That it will be easy for them, surely not, but I'm of the opinion that it's better to try and not succeed than to have your whole life pass in thinking:

177
00:28:35.010 --> 00:28:40.970
what would have happened if I had tried, maybe I would have succeeded, maybe not.

178
00:28:40.970 --> 00:28:49.080
I'm of the view that everyone who has some idea should start on realizing it.

179
00:28:49.080 --> 00:28:56.990
Financially, when I started here, it was not a good moment at all.

180
00:28:56.990 --> 00:29:06.030
Nothing was easy, but, let's say, everything was sweet. In that struggle a person enjoys a lot.

181
00:29:10.990 --> 00:29:15.440
Now, after everything you've been through, are you happy?

182
00:29:15.440 --> 00:29:26.130
Srđan once lived at a rushed city pace, and today he breathes with full lungs, surrounded by horses, mountains and silence.

183
00:29:26.130 --> 00:29:37.390
He is proof that happiness depends on courage, on how ready we are for big steps to change our lives for the better.

184
00:29:37.390 --> 00:29:43.630
He found the peace that many are looking for, and few really find.
